"*minor* — API yang sempit; hanya memengaruhi skrip yang menggunakannya."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:99
msgid "*behavior* — same API, different results; re-check tuned scripts."
msgstr ""
"*behavior* — API sama, hasil berbeda; periksa kembali skrip yang telah "
"disetel."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:101
msgid ""
"Changes are grouped by impact in that order. If you just want to port your "
"code, jump to the :ref:`migration checklist <v3_0_0_migration>` at the end. "
"Each commit hash links to its diff on GitHub."
msgstr ""
"Perubahan dikelompokkan berdasarkan dampak dalam urutan tersebut. Jika Anda "
"hanya ingin melakukan porting kode, langsung ke :ref:`daftar periksa migrasi"
" <v3_0_0_migration>` di bagian akhir. Setiap hash commit terhubung ke diff-"
"nya di GitHub."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:108
msgid ""
"``image.find_number()`` / ``image.classify_object()`` removed *(major)*"
msgstr ""
"``image.find_number()`` / ``image.classify_object()`` dihapus *(major)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:110
msgid ""
"The hard-coded ``image.find_number()`` (LeNet) and "
"``image.classify_object()`` (CMSIS CNN) methods were removed in favor of the"
" new ``nn`` module. Replace them with ``net = nn.load('/model.network'); out"
" = net.forward(img)``."
msgstr ""
"Metode hard-coded ``image.find_number()`` (LeNet) dan "
"``image.classify_object()`` (CMSIS CNN) telah dihapus demi modul ``nn`` yang"
" baru. Gantikan dengan ``net = nn.load('/model.network'); out = "
"net.forward(img)``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:115
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `d151f7e38 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/d151f7e38>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `d151f7e38 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/d151f7e38>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:120
msgid ":func:`sensor.sleep` / :func:`sensor.reset` raise on failure *(minor)*"
msgstr ""
":func:`sensor.sleep` / :func:`sensor.reset` melempar pengecualian saat gagal"
" *(minor)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:122
msgid ""
":func:`sensor.sleep` and :func:`sensor.reset` now raise an exception on "
"failure instead of returning ``True`` / ``False``. Code that checked the "
"boolean return of :func:`sensor.sleep` must wrap the call in ``try`` / "
"``except`` instead."
msgstr ""
":func:`sensor.sleep` dan :func:`sensor.reset` kini melempar pengecualian "
"saat gagal alih-alih mengembalikan ``True`` / ``False``\\ . Kode yang "
"memeriksa nilai boolean dari :func:`sensor.sleep` harus membungkus panggilan"
" dalam ``try`` / ``except``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:127
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `7d16d008f <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/7d16d008f>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `7d16d008f <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/7d16d008f>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:132
msgid "WINC sockets return the real byte count *(behavior)*"
msgstr "Socket WINC mengembalikan jumlah byte sebenarnya *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:134
msgid ""
"The WINC1500 socket ``send`` / ``recv`` / ``sendto`` / ``recvfrom`` methods "
"previously always returned ``0``; they now return the actual number of bytes"
" transferred. Code that assumed a ``0`` return (or looped/blocked on it) "
"must handle the real counts."
msgstr ""
"Metode ``send`` / ``recv`` / ``sendto`` / ``recvfrom`` pada socket WINC1500 "
"sebelumnya selalu mengembalikan ``0``\\ ; kini mengembalikan jumlah byte "
"yang sebenarnya ditransfer. Kode yang mengasumsikan kembalian ``0`` (atau "
"melakukan loop/blokir padanya) harus menangani jumlah byte yang sebenarnya."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:139
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `a07fb2f60 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/a07fb2f60>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `a07fb2f60 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/a07fb2f60>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:144
msgid "``image.binary()`` returns a new image *(behavior)*"
msgstr "``image.binary()`` mengembalikan citra baru *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:146
msgid ""
"``image.binary()`` gained ``to_bitmap`` / ``copy`` keywords and now returns "
"a new image object instead of returning/mutating the source image in place. "
"Code that relied on ``binary()`` mutating the original image should use the "
"returned object (and pass ``copy=True`` for non-in-place behavior)."
msgstr ""
"``image.binary()`` mendapatkan kata kunci ``to_bitmap`` / ``copy`` dan kini "
"mengembalikan objek citra baru alih-alih mengembalikan/memutasi citra sumber"
" secara in-place. Kode yang mengandalkan ``binary()`` untuk memutasi citra "
"asli harus menggunakan objek yang dikembalikan (dan meneruskan ``copy=True``"
" untuk perilaku non-in-place)."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:151
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `8a44f0cd9 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/8a44f0cd9>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `8a44f0cd9 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/8a44f0cd9>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:156
msgid "``find_apriltags()`` capped at 64K pixels *(behavior)*"
msgstr "``find_apriltags()`` dibatasi pada 64K piksel *(behavior)*"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:158
msgid ""
"``image.find_apriltags()`` now raises if the image (or ROI) exceeds 64K "
"pixels and returns an empty list for images smaller than 4x4. Downscale "
"large images (use a smaller ``framesize`` or pass an explicit ``roi``) "
"before calling ``find_apriltags()``."
msgstr ""
"``image.find_apriltags()`` kini melempar pengecualian jika citra (atau ROI) "
"melebihi 64K piksel dan mengembalikan daftar kosong untuk citra yang lebih "
"kecil dari 4x4. Perkecil citra besar (gunakan ``framesize`` yang lebih kecil"
" atau teruskan ``roi`` eksplisit) sebelum memanggil ``find_apriltags()``\\ ."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:163
msgid ""
"*Commits:* `bd77afbc0 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/bd77afbc0>`__"
msgstr ""
"*Commit:* `bd77afbc0 <https://github.com/openmv/openmv/commit/bd77afbc0>`__"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:168
msgid "Migration checklist"
msgstr "Daftar periksa migrasi"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:170
msgid "For a clean port to v3.0.0 the typical work is:"
msgstr "Untuk porting yang bersih ke v3.0.0, pekerjaan umumnya adalah:"

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:172
msgid ""
"Replace ``image.find_number()`` / ``image.classify_object()`` with the "
"``nn`` module (:ref:`the nn migration <v3_0_0_nn>`)."
msgstr ""
"Gantikan ``image.find_number()`` / ``image.classify_object()`` dengan modul "
"``nn`` (\\ :ref:`migrasi nn <v3_0_0_nn>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:174
msgid ""
"Wrap :func:`sensor.sleep` / :func:`sensor.reset` in ``try`` / ``except`` "
"instead of checking a boolean return (:ref:`the sensor.sleep change "
"<v3_0_0_sleep>`)."
msgstr ""
"Bungkus :func:`sensor.sleep` / :func:`sensor.reset` dalam ``try`` / "
"``except`` alih-alih memeriksa nilai boolean (\\ :ref:`perubahan "
"sensor.sleep <v3_0_0_sleep>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:177
msgid ""
"Handle real byte counts from WINC socket ``send`` / ``recv`` (:ref:`the WINC"
" socket change <v3_0_0_winc>`)."
msgstr ""
"Tangani jumlah byte sebenarnya dari socket WINC ``send`` / ``recv`` (\\ "
":ref:`perubahan socket WINC <v3_0_0_winc>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:179
msgid ""
"Use the image returned by ``image.binary()`` instead of expecting in-place "
"mutation (:ref:`the binary change <v3_0_0_binary>`)."
msgstr ""
"Gunakan citra yang dikembalikan oleh ``image.binary()`` alih-alih "
"mengharapkan mutasi in-place (\\ :ref:`perubahan binary <v3_0_0_binary>`\\ "
")."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:181
msgid ""
"Downscale images before ``find_apriltags()`` to stay under 64K pixels "
"(:ref:`the find_apriltags cap <v3_0_0_apriltags>`)."
msgstr ""
"Perkecil citra sebelum ``find_apriltags()`` agar tetap di bawah 64K piksel "
"(\\ :ref:`batas find_apriltags <v3_0_0_apriltags>`\\ )."

#: ../../changelog/firmware/v3.0.0.rst:184
msgid "All other scripts run unchanged."
msgstr "Semua skrip lainnya berjalan tanpa perubahan."
